A||||13||JetroGT||PARK. Not good to stop your car with.||||1||
Z||000000||JetroGT||11-17-2000||06:20 AM||||I was talking about selling my black SE at work today and replacing it with another Blue GT. <BR>One of my coworkers wanted to know more about the car I was selling so out on break I let him drive it around the parking lot. This guy is probably well over 6 feet tall. Getting in he bumps his head, but once in the car, no problems. He backs the car out then puts it in to drive.<BR>We're going along for a bit then he wants to check the brakes. "Fiero brakes are usually a<BR>little spongy". He's stepping on the brakes and says, I can't stop! I can't stop! Then he puts it into park! I hear the tranny grinding as I'm yelling, "What are you doing!", then it rocks to a stop. I'm thinking, "Should I make him get out? Anyway, I felt better when I watched <BR>him try to get out of the car. He wants to get a car for his 16 year old cousin. I'm thinking mabie he should get a big old caddy for a starter car. I'm not nocking the fiero, it's just that when your 16 you tend to tear up your first car. At least I did. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||overlord||11-17-2000||07:57 AM||||geez!||||reg||1
