Z||000003||stsmithgt||11-17-2000||09:53 AM||||Don't you just hate it when you think someone knows what their doing and then you pay the price to find out..DOH!  It doesn't sound like anything broke since it did stop.  If you keep your ears open at a grocery store parking lot, you'll here that same niose fairly often.  (notice I didn't blame it on women?)  My flame suit is at the cleaners)<BR>I vaporized a "park" in a Galaxy 500 I had back in the 80's over a dare.  You don't stop when going over a hundred and throw it into park.  Ahhh, the younger days when there is plenty of time to pull a tranny for the hell of it. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  You should have seen their eyes when they saw me grap the shifter and tossed it into park. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> moo hoo hoo ha ha ha.||||reg||13
Z||000004||fldevel||11-17-2000||10:51 AM||||i resent the 16 year old remark ..i still have the same car sence i was 16 i am now 20 ..that was my red 2m4 it still runs but needs new crank berings .. and how can you not stop a fiero ?? just open the door and use the sole of your shoe if your breaks go out ...||||reg||1
Z||000005||turbo86se||11-17-2000||12:18 PM||||LOL, that reminds me of when I tried to sell my first Fiero, an 85 2m4 5-spd. This was a long time ago, but a kid, maybe 16 or 17 came out to drive it. The clutch was a little tricky, but certainly drivable. I also had the Fi-euro shifter I got at IRM. I drove first and sped through all the gears, then he drove it, WOW, it's a miracle the tranny didn't fall out!! He grinded every gear, dumped the clutch, stalled it several times, at one point I thought the tranny DID fall out, I heard and felt this huge slam! I told him that's enough and to get out. No real damage was done, thank goodness!!<BR>No way was I going to let him buy my Fiero!! ||||reg||10
Z||000006||Phil||11-17-2000||12:39 PM||||I think I can do ya one better - My brother just sold his '87 Porsche 924S(37K miles) to a 16 year old kid that doesn't know how to drive a stick and when the kid expressed an additional concern about driving in the snow his father said "Well we'll just put chains on it" Sadly the father was serious. My brother and I just kinda looked at each other as the man and his son drove off in their new BMW.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Richard Parnell||11-17-2000||03:00 PM||||I just recently completed a v8 swap in my 87 sc and have been driving it all over.  Well, my neighbor (a sexy Panamanian babe) expressed a desire in driving my car when I gave her a ride in it.  I thought what the hell, she drives sports cars and she saw how I was coddling the clutch which I told her had to be broken in a bit slowly for the first 500 miles or so.  Well, I pull over out on this country road and she gets in the drivers seat adjusts the seat, Revs the car up and proceeds to dump the clutch, slam the gas and bang throught the first 4 gears until we're doing around  100 or so.  I couldn't believe it.  I looked over at her with my mouth hanging open and she's going "Wow this is great I could get into this."  I then realized that the passenger side of a Fiero doesn't have a chicken bar to hang onto.  She finally slowed down behind some cars we came up behind and cruised for a few minutes until we came to a straight away.  She proceeded to pass all the cars in front of us and finally got up into 5th gear about which time she had to work the brakes (which are in sore need of replacement) like mad to make the turn at the end of the straight away.  We went flying past the nursing home which I was thinking about then that I'd never live to be such a ripe old age to have use of and we finally came to our street where she whipped into my drivemay.  I tumbled out of the car a told her she's downright dangerous and I hoped she never got anything larger than a 4 cyl engine in her next car (her present 300zx is dead, I wonder why).  My legs were actually shaking.  If she weren't so danmed good looking I'd have spanked her.  Actually that sounds like a good idea and I should go over next door a give a good tanning right now.||||reg||11
Z||000008||JetroGT||11-17-2000||07:58 PM||||I'm sorry if anyone was offended by the younger driver remark. I was just rembering when I was 16. Practically killing myself on a regular basis. Anyway, I won't be selling my SE yet any way. The auto 87 Blue GT I was going to by was not in the best of shape. If any one is interested I was looking on the yahoo classifieds, using 76180 as a zip code. Now they only want $2500. for it. They live in Lancaster, TX. That's south Dallas. ||||reg||11
Z||000009||Seanh||11-17-2000||10:06 PM||||Hey, I was just wondering about that chain remark in a previous post on the Porsche. Why would that be a bad thing, or did you intend for it to be? I'm stupid, and not really sure what is bad about chains. I dont know if I should say this or not, but I drove my Fiero last weekend with, umm. Ch-Cha-Chains on it. Is that not a good thing? It was the only way to get around.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
